\section{Distributed Training}
\label{sec:distributed}
% ================================================================

\subsection{Architecture}

Distributed training across $N$ GPUs uses a
\emph{data-parallel delta-averaging} strategy:

\begin{algorithm}
\caption{RSF Distributed Training Step (rank $r$)}
\label{alg:dist}
\begin{algorithmic}[1]
  \State $\theta_0 \leftarrow \text{snapshot of current weights}$
  \State Run local SGD update: $\theta_r \leftarrow \text{LocalStep}(\theta_0, \text{batch}_r)$
  \State $\Delta_r \leftarrow \theta_r - \theta_0$
  \State $\bar\Delta \leftarrow \frac{1}{N}\texttt{allReduce}(\sum_r \Delta_r)$ \Comment{NCCL}
  \State $\theta \leftarrow \theta_0 + \bar\Delta$ \Comment{applied on all ranks}
\end{algorithmic}
\end{algorithm}

This approach synchronises only \emph{deltas} rather than full
weight tensors, reducing communication volume while maintaining
convergence guarantees equivalent to synchronous SGD.

