\subsection{Dataset Sharding}

The trainer counts valid JSON lines in the dataset, computes
\texttt{samples\_per\_rank} $= \lfloor N_{\text{total}} / N_{\text{ranks}} \rfloor$,
and each rank loads only its assigned shard by seeking to
\texttt{start\_valid\_index}.
This avoids replicating the full dataset in CPU memory on every node.

\subsection{Hybrid Quantum Extension}

An experimental \texttt{DistributedTrainer} variant
(\texttt{trainEpochHybrid}) interleaves classical \RSF{} layers with
quantum circuit executions.
The \texttt{QuantumTrainingConfig} specifies the IBM CRN backend,
number of VQE layers, and shot budget.
Metrics tracked include circuit depth, gate fidelity estimates,
and shot noise variance per step.
While this hybrid mode remains experimental, it demonstrates the
extensibility of the \RSF{} framework to emerging hardware paradigms.

